   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; On Jan 24, 2017, at 5:22 AM, Andrew O&#39;Reilly-Nugent &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">pers...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Simple question hopefully begets a simple answer: can I vectorise this model further?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "No, but switching it to use correlation matrix Cholesky factors\r<br>rather than correlation matrices will be a lot faster and more\r<br>arithmetically stable.  There&#39;s an example in the regression chapter\r<br>of the manual.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "1XDNB9AqDAAJ",
   "from": "Andrew O'Reilly-Nugent",
   "author": "27daa73cdb503da4",
   "date": "2017-01-29T21:14:09Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Vectorising array of covariance matrices",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Bob! One more question: what&#39;s the appropriate way to initialise an array of Cholesky factors?<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve tried passing in both a list of J x J matrices, and a 3D array with dimensions [N_sp, J, J] to no avail. Another answer on this list suggested that lists of matrices could not be passed in from R.</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "GI-nKXcwDAAJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2017-01-29T22:57:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Vectorising array of covariance matrices",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Sunday, January 29, 2017 at 4:14:09 PM UTC-5, Andrew O&#39;Reilly-Nugent wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Bob! One more question: what&#39;s the appropriate way to initialise an array of Cholesky factors?<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve tried passing in both a list of J x J matrices, and a 3D array with dimensions [N_sp, J, J] to no avail. Another answer on this list suggested that lists of matrices could not be passed in from R.</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>This was fixed on GitHub. <br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "J7b_GgdDDAAJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2017-01-30T04:37:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Vectorising array of covariance matrices",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Yes, it should be N x J x J coming in as matrices (that is,\r<br>with zeros filled in above the diagonal).    We validate\r<br>that they really are Cholesky factors for positive definite\r<br>or correlation matrices.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; On Jan 29, 2017, at 4:14 PM, Andrew O&#39;Reilly-Nugent &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">pers...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Thanks Bob! One more question: what&#39;s the appropriate way to initialise an array of Cholesky factors?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I&#39;ve tried passing in both a list of J x J matrices, and a 3D array with dimensions [N_sp, J, J] to no avail. Another answer on this list suggested that lists of matrices could not be passed in from R.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
